\formshade\paperh15840\paperw12240\margl1134\margr1134\margt1134\margb1134\sectd\sbknone\sectunlocked1\pgndec\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1134\margrsxn1134\margtsxn1134\margbsxn1134\ftnbj\ftnstart1\ftnrstcont\ftnnar\aenddoc\aftnrstcont\aftnstart1\aftnnrlc
\pgndec\pard\plain \s1\ilvl0\outlinelevel0\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs48\ab\loch\f3\fs48\sb240\sa120{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Living Notitia: From a Late Roman Register to an Interactive Information System}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Notitia Dignitatum}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
\~ is one of the most remarkable administrative documents to survive from the Roman world. Compiled around the turn of the fifth century, it is essentially a register of the senior offices of the late Roman Empire. It covers both the eastern and western halves of the empire and lists civil officials, military commands, administrative territories, army units, staffs, arsenals and other institutions belonging to the imperial state.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
At first sight, however, the Notitia is not an especially inviting text. It does not tell a story. It does not explain how the Roman state worked. It simply lists things.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A typical section begins with an official \uc3 \u8212\'e2\'80\'94 a\~ \uc1 }{\*\cs16\i\ai\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
praefectus}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
,\~ }{\*\cs16\i\ai\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
vicarius}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
,\~ }{\*\cs16\i\ai\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
comes}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
,\~ }{\*\cs16\i\ai\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
dux}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
\~ or some other office-holder \uc3 \u8212\'e2\'80\'94 and continues with the provinces, subordinate officials, military units or members of staff under that person's authority. Elsewhere it enumerates provinces belonging to a larger administrative region, units stationed at particular places, or factories and other establishments under an imperial department.\uc1 }
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
For a modern reader, it can therefore look like a rather repetitive catalogue of Latin names and titles.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The starting point of\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Living Notitia}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
\~ was the suspicion that this apparent dullness is misleading. The repetitive character of the text is precisely what makes it interesting. The Notitia is not merely prose describing an administration. It is, in an important sense, the surviving output of an\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
information system}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Reading the Notitia as structured information}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The essential idea behind Living Notitia was to stop treating the Notitia primarily as a text to be read from beginning to end and instead ask what sort of information structure lies behind it.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A modern organisation might maintain databases containing organisations, offices, employees, geographic areas, reporting relationships and locations. The Romans obviously had no electronic database, but their administration nevertheless had to manage many of the same kinds of relationships.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
An official exercised authority over a particular territory. A province belonged to a larger administrative region. A military commander controlled particular units. A unit could be associated with a named place. An office contained a staff with a recognisable set of functions. Imperial factories and financial offices belonged to their respective administrative hierarchies.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The Notitia preserves many of these relationships.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
What is striking is the regularity with which they appear. The same forms recur throughout the document. Titles introduce sections. Groups of subordinate items follow them. Formulaic expressions indicate that something is "under the authority of" an official. Geographic lists use recurring patterns. Staff lists belonging to quite different offices often contain similar functions.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Once this was noticed, a different question became possible:}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Could the structure implicit in the Latin text be made explicit, without replacing the Latin text with a modern reconstruction?}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
That became the central principle of Living Notitia.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The Latin text as the authority}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
From an early stage, we made an important methodological decision:\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
the Latin text itself would remain the authoritative source}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
This sounds obvious, but it has major consequences.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
It would have been relatively easy to begin with a modern historical map of the Roman Empire and construct a database of provinces, cities, governors and military units from modern reference works. That might produce a useful historical database, but it would no longer be a model of the Notitia Dignitatum itself.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Living Notitia takes the opposite approach.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The modern database must emerge from the text.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
If the Notitia says that a particular unit belongs under a particular commander, that relationship can be represented. If it names a place, the place can become an entity in the model. If it groups provinces under an administrative heading, that grouping can be represented. But the system should not silently add a relationship simply because modern historians know that it ought to exist.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Modern scholarship, Wikipedia, Pleiades and geographic data can be attached later as additional information. They are extremely useful for identifying places, obtaining coordinates and comparing ancient and modern geography. But they are auxiliary layers.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The Latin remains the "gold standard".}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
This distinction has proved more important than we initially expected. Ancient place names are often ambiguous. The same name can occur in several parts of the Roman world. Spellings vary. A name can refer to a town in one context and a wider territory in another. Modern databases sometimes identify places differently from the way the Notitia appears to use them.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Instead of hiding these discrepancies, Living Notitia can expose them.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
That turns errors and uncertainties into historical evidence.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
From document to model}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The first experiments were remarkably simple.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
We began with electronic versions of the Latin texts of the\~ }{\*\cs16\i\ai\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Notitia Occidentis}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
\~ and\~ }{\*\cs16\i\ai\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Notitia Orientis}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
. Rather than trying immediately to "understand" every sentence, we looked first at their visible structure.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The text contains chapters, headings, lists and repeated formulas. Some entries introduce groups; others clearly belong underneath them. Certain phrases function almost like markers indicating that a new administrative block is beginning.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The more closely we examined the text, the more it began to resemble a hierarchical data structure.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
This changed the project.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Initially, one might have imagined extracting names from the Notitia: officials, provinces, places and units. But extraction alone loses something crucial. A name by itself is not very informative. What matters is its\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
context}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A military unit is interesting because it belongs to a particular command. A province is interesting because it occurs within a particular administrative structure. A place is interesting because the text associates something with that place.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Consequently, the project evolved from a collection of extracted names into a model preserving the hierarchy of the original source.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
At the lowest level stands the individual line or entry of the Notitia. Above it are the groups, sections and chapters in which that entry occurs. Alongside this textual structure we can identify semantic categories such as office, province, place, military unit or function.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The result is not a translation of the Notitia. Nor is it simply a transcription.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
It is an attempt to represent the\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
logic of the document}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The role of the AI dialogue}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Living Notitia did not begin with a finished specification.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
It emerged through an extended dialogue between a human reader and an AI.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
That is an important part of the project.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The process was highly iterative. We would examine a passage of the Notitia, formulate a hypothesis about its structure, write a small program to test the hypothesis against the whole text, inspect the result, discover exceptions, and modify the model.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Again and again, apparently minor observations changed the direction of the work.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A line that initially looked like ordinary prose would turn out to behave like the end marker of a group. A repeated Latin formula would reveal that dozens of sections followed the same structural pattern. A supposed place name would prove to be a province or region. An apparent anomaly in the map would expose a problem in the way the text had been classified rather than a problem with the geography.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
This is where the conversational nature of AI became particularly useful.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Traditional programming generally begins with a specification: decide what the program is supposed to do, write the program, and test it.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Living Notitia often worked in the reverse direction.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
We did not always know what the correct data model was because discovering that model was itself part of the historical investigation.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The conversation could therefore move rapidly between several different modes:}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
reading Latin;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
discussing Roman administration;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
examining the structure of a manuscript or transcription;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
proposing a data model;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
writing a short Python script;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
inspecting thousands of resulting entries;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
noticing inconsistencies;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
and returning to the Latin source to see what had gone wrong.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The AI was therefore not simply being used to generate code. Code generation was useful, but it was only one part of the process.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The more interesting function was the continuous movement between\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
textual interpretation and computational testing}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A proposed interpretation could be tested against the entire Notitia in seconds. If it worked in ten examples but failed in two hundred others, the hypothesis was probably wrong. Conversely, patterns that would have been extremely tedious to identify manually became visible once the whole text could be classified and counted.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The dialogue gradually turned into a form of collaborative source criticism.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
An important change of perspective}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
One of the most useful discoveries was that we did not have to understand everything at once.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Early attempts naturally tried to classify every line as an office, unit, province, function, place or some other category. But the Notitia is complicated, and premature classification creates errors.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A more productive strategy was to separate several questions.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
First:}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
What is the structure of the source?}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Then:}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
What does each element appear to represent?}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
And finally:}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
What relationships can safely be inferred from its context?}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
This separation allowed the text to remain intact even when its interpretation was uncertain.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
An entry can exist in the system before we know exactly what kind of entry it is. Later, improved classification can change its semantic interpretation without altering the underlying source.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
That principle is fundamental to Living Notitia.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The source and the interpretation are not the same thing.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Geography as a test case}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Geography became one of the most revealing parts of the project.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The Notitia contains hundreds of ancient geographic names: provinces, regions, towns, forts and other places. By comparing these with modern geographic datasets such as\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Pleiades}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
, many of them can be given coordinates and displayed on a map.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
At first this might appear to be a straightforward matching problem: take the ancient name in the Notitia, find the corresponding name in Pleiades, obtain latitude and longitude, and place a marker on the map.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
In practice it is much more interesting.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Some names match immediately. Others have different spellings. Some occur more than once in the ancient world. Some entries that look like places are actually regions or administrative descriptions. And occasionally a plausible automatic match puts a Roman place hundreds or thousands of kilometres from the province in which the Notitia places it.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Those failures are useful.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Because the web application knows something about the administrative context of an entry, a geographic match can be checked against that context. A place associated with a unit in Britannia should normally be in or near Britannia. A supposed match in Syria is therefore immediately suspicious even if the name happens to resemble the Latin name.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
This creates a powerful combination of textual and geographic evidence.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The map is not merely an illustration attached to the text. It becomes a method for checking the interpretation of the text.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
From research experiment to web application}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
As the underlying model became more stable, the project naturally developed into a web application.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The objective was not to build another digital edition in which the user searches for a Latin word and receives a page of text.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The aim was to make the administrative structure\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
navigable}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The user should be able to begin high in the hierarchy, open a section, move through the administrative levels and eventually arrive at an individual office, military unit, function or place.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
At the same time, the user should never lose contact with the source.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
This led to the basic architecture of the Living Notitia interface.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
One part of the screen presents the hierarchical structure of the document. An inspector can show what is known about the selected entry: its Latin text, its place in the source, its classification and its administrative context. A map can show the relevant province or place.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The result allows several views of the same evidence to coexist.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A line in a fifth-century administrative register can simultaneously be seen as:}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
a piece of Latin text;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
an element of a manuscript structure;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
an administrative entity;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
part of a hierarchy;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
a geographic reference;}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af5\dbch\af5\loch\f5 \'95\tab}\ilvl0\ls2 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0\widctlpar\tx707\li707\ri0\lin707\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
and a node connected to other pieces of information.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
None of these replaces the others.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Together they make the document easier to explore.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A "living" Notitia}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
This is the reason for the name\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Living Notitia}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The intention is not to modernise the Roman Empire or pretend that the Notitia was literally a modern database. It is to allow the relationships contained in a static ancient document to become active and explorable.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A printed edition necessarily presents information sequentially. Page 50 follows page 49.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A digital model need not work that way.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A user interested in Britannia can enter through Britannia. Someone studying military organisation can follow commanders and units. Someone interested in provincial administration can follow dioceses and provinces. Someone investigating a particular ancient place can examine every context in which the Notitia refers to it.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Eventually it should also be possible to move in the opposite direction: from a point on the map to the relevant passage of the Notitia.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The underlying text has not changed.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
What changes is the reader's ability to move through it.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
AI as an interface to the source}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
There is also a further possibility.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Once the Notitia has been represented as structured information, AI can become an interface to the document itself.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Instead of knowing the exact Latin wording or database field required for a search, a user might ask ordinary questions:}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Which military units in the Notitia are associated with Britain?}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Which provinces belong under the Vicarius of the Diocese of Pontica?}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Where does the title\~ }{\*\cs16\i\ai\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
dux}{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
\~ occur in the western empire?}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Which places mentioned in the Notitia cannot confidently be matched to Pleiades?}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The important point is that the AI should not answer such questions simply from its general knowledge of Roman history.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
It should interrogate the Living Notitia data and distinguish clearly between what the source actually says and what is supplied by modern interpretation.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
In that sense, the project comes full circle.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
AI helped turn the Latin text into an information model. The information model can now allow AI to become a much more disciplined way of interrogating the Latin text.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb240\sa120\keepn\b\hich\af6\dbch\af6\afs36\ab\loch\f3\fs36\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
What Living Notitia is really about}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Living Notitia began as an experiment in making an ancient administrative document easier to explore. It has gradually become something broader.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
It is an experiment in\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
digital historical method}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The project asks what happens when we take the formal structure of an ancient source seriously enough to model it rather than merely transcribe it.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The Notitia Dignitatum is particularly suitable because its repetitive, bureaucratic character exposes the underlying administrative structure unusually clearly. But the approach need not be limited to the Notitia.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Tax registers, legal records, papyri, ecclesiastical lists, military records and other apparently monotonous historical sources may contain similar hidden structures.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
These documents were produced because administrations needed to store, organise and retrieve information.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
If their internal organisation can be recovered, they can sometimes be treated not simply as collections of sentences but as remnants of historical information systems.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
That perspective also changes what AI is good for.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The most interesting use of AI in Living Notitia has not been asking it to write a history of the late Roman Empire. Plenty of such histories already exist.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Its value has been in the repeated cycle of\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
observation, hypothesis, modelling, testing and correction}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
A human reader notices that something looks significant. AI helps formulate and implement a way to test it. The computer applies that test to thousands of lines. The unexpected results lead the human back to the source.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Neither side is particularly remarkable in isolation.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The interesting result comes from the dialogue between them.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
Living Notitia is the product of that dialogue: a fifth-century Roman administrative register, preserved as Latin text, gradually transformed into an interactive model while keeping the ancient source at the centre.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
The goal is not to make the Notitia say more than it says.}
\par \pard\plain \s19\sb0\sa120\widctlpar\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi0{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
It is to make more of what it already contains\~ }{\*\cs15\b\ab\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
visible}{\scaps0\caps0\cf1\expnd0\expndtw0\i0\b0\rtlch \ltrch\loch
.}
